{"t":1794362549806,"type":"say","kind":"delivered","why":"The reply presents finished results: a voiceover file and a music bed file, each with a download link. It adds caveats (no tool to mix the audio, links expire after 24 hours) but does not ask for a choice, approval, or refuse. It also gives mixing steps for the user to combine the files.","called":true,"text":"I need to be upfront: Magic Hour has no tool that mixes a voice over music. So I couldn't give you one finished file. Instead I made the two parts, ready for you to combine:\n\n1. Voiceover: \"Hazel\", a warm female voice, reads your script word for word (11 credits):\nhttps://videos.magichour.ai/cmwbh1zqe048uh401sjcvonyp/output.wav?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=web-service%40magic-hour-385504.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261111%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261111T020026Z&X-Goog-Expires=86400&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-\n\n2. Music bed: 20 seconds of upbeat, gentle electronic music with no vocals. I asked for a short music-only opening and a fade at the end (20 credits):\nhttps://videos.magichour.ai/cmwbh22hc048cf10110298yxm/output.wav?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=web-service%40magic-hour-385504.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261111%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261111T020051Z&X-Goog-Expires=86400&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-\n\nTo combine them, use any free audio editor, such as Audacity or GarageBand:\n- Put the music on one track, starting at 0:00.\n- Put the voice on a second track, starting at about 0:03. That leaves the music-only opening.\n- Turn the music down about 10–15 dB while the voice plays, so the voice stays clear.\n- Export the result as one MP3 or WAV.\n\nThe links stop working after 24 hours, so download both files soon. I can also try a different voice or music style if you like."}
